  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "t6m8AkMHD9IUAeUwl6X8/xfUAHI=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:38.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "`github.com/powerhouse-inc/recipes` holds 21 standalone projects, each a clonable-and-runnable demonstration of one Reactor pattern. The Cookbook's recipe table and its per-recipe detail sections are **auto-generated** from that repo by `scripts/generate-recipe-docs.ts` \u2014 the academy markdown carries an explicit \"do not edit directly\" marker \u2014 so the repo, not the docs, is the source of truth.\n\nGrouped by what they teach:\n\n| Theme | Recipes |\n| --- | --- |\n| Read models & projection | analytics-processor, custom-read-model, full-text-search, semantic-search, relational-db-subgraph |\n| Cross-document automation | cross-document-reactor, saga, batch-progress |\n| External integrations | external-feed-ingest, inbound-webhook-bridge, discord-webhook-processor |\n| Identity, auth & limits | role-based-auth, signed-operations-verifier, rate-limiter, audit-trail |\n| Sync & ops | sync-health-monitor, subscription-cli, db-migrate, document-snapshot-exporter |\n| Schema evolution & containers | document-versioning, drive-override |\n\nSeveral are the *only* documentation of their subject at any depth \u2014 `document-versioning` on the `initialState` replay trap, `inbound-webhook-bridge` on raw-bytes HMAC verification, `drive-override` on `ADD_RELATIONSHIP` scaling. Where the reference docs and a recipe overlap, the recipe usually carries the failure mode and the test that proves it.\n\nTwo properties make them unusually citable. Most run **fully offline** on an in-process PGlite-backed reactor with no external services, and most **generate their document models from a committed spec** via `ph generate document-model --document <spec>.json` with a pinned `ph-cli`, so the codegen output in the repo matches a known toolchain version. Several also pair a demo (`pnpm start`) with a test suite that asserts the pathological case rather than just the happy path.\n\nRecipes are AGPL-3.0-only where licensing is stated.\n\nProvenance: academy `05-Lookup/00-Cookbook.md`, \"Reactor Recipes\" section (auto-generated block), academy 6.2.2-dev.45.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T12:35:38.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:38.000Z"
    }
  },
